{number: 138}
{title: Where Jesus Is,’Tis Heaven}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Since [C] Christ my soul from sin set free,
This world has [F] been a heaven to [C] me;
And 'mid earth's sorrows and its woe,
'Tis [G7] heaven my Savior here to [C] know.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O [F] hallelujah, yes, 'tis [C] heaven,
'Tis heaven to know my sins for-[G7] given;
On [C] land or sea, what-[F] e'er be-[C] fall,
Where Jesus [G7] is, 'tis heaven for [C] all.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Once [C] earth seemed dark and full of gloom,
Now [F] flowers of joy and peace a-[C] bloom;
The clouds are gone, the sky is clear,
Since [G7] Jesus came and brought me [C] cheer.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
'Tis [C] heaven to walk with Him each day,
'Tis [F] heaven to hear Him softly [C] say,
"Fear not, My child, I'm by thy side,"
In [G7] Him my soul is satis-[C] fied.
{end_of_verse}
